  "about": "The English messages the Automations move's pure rules introduced (src/core/i18n/en.ts, automations.*), each with sample values. test/unit/i18n/moved-strings.test.ts asserts that the French catalog renders what the rewrite layer makes of the English or, where the layer leaves the English or gets it wrong (`Turn on` is `Turn : activé`), the `translated` French. Nothing visible changes in #271 and #272: the legacy panel draws these messages in English (tEn in src/auto.js) and the layer still translates them as before; the translated rows became visible when #273 drew the tab in the panel's language, with its baselines, and added the pane's own messages below. #273 also deleted the layer's entries only the tab used: their rows are `was` rows, with the French the layer made of them.",
